{"action_id":null,"arguments":[],"assumptions":[{"assumption_id":"node.68f8e39cf8e43c95a1e0890d.a0","provenance_refs":[],"statement":"The formalization evaluates one particular fund at one identified assessment time; it does not determine whole-firm compliance or satisfaction of the downstream sales requirements.","status":"PROVISIONAL"},{"assumption_id":"node.68f8e39cf8e43c95a1e0890d.a1","provenance_refs":[],"statement":"Footnote 6 qualifies the defined population of Funds, and footnote 7 qualifies the holistic designation assessment in cases below 50%.","status":"PROVISIONAL"},{"assumption_id":"node.68f8e39cf8e43c95a1e0890d.a2","provenance_refs":[],"statement":"The designation fact records an actual, applicable SFC designation. A manager's view that designation is likely or appropriate does not establish that fact.","status":"PROVISIONAL"},{"assumption_id":"node.68f8e39cf8e43c95a1e0890d.a3","provenance_refs":[],"statement":"The threshold fact must be established using a supportable exposure measurement. The formalization supplies no missing valuation, look-through, aggregation or monitoring convention.","status":"PROVISIONAL"},{"assumption_id":"node.68f8e39cf8e43c95a1e0890d.a4","provenance_refs":[],"statement":"A result is interpreted only within the Boolean scope. Unknown facts are not assigned false values; one established true classification route can nevertheless establish the result without resolving the other route.","status":"PROVISIONAL"}],"bundle_hash":"c7b206d931f70fc417bcc9d7047a159b7d37bd54e34ff128260703ab058cc295","candidate_id":"candidate.fa23b07644bf4e6a93f871967e99f02d","controlled_language":"[TRUE_IS_SATISFIED] For an SFC-authorised fund offered to the public in Hong Kong that is not a listed closed-ended alternative asset fund, the classification trigger is satisfied when its aggregate direct and indirect exposure to private market assets is at least 50% of NAV, or when the SFC has actually designated it as a complex product on a case-by-case basis. True means that this circular supplies a basis requiring complex-product treatment for distribution. False, within scope and with the relevant facts established, means that neither classification route is established under this selected control; it does not establish non-complex status under every other applicable rule. Missing exposure or designation evidence remains unknown. The retained text supports one classification structure; the principal unresolved issues concern exposure measurement, timing and evidence, rather than a competing rule making every private-market exposure automatically complex.","disposition_reason":"Unreviewed interpretation proposal","family_ids":["modality"],"generation_phase":"BLIND_INITIAL","issue_ids":["issue.82babbfd9df9475689c45643510d106d","issue.ffa32b54b207412cac159c55d3ef64ef","issue.3c9cc2935d4b4456bf3e984246919c36","issue.5e877b83fdf44d4d928c103b59294543","issue.f5ea4672169648f98cf192d06c86196b"],"parent_id":null,"probability_of_legal_correctness":null,"revision_reason":"The threshold sentence uses mandatory language, while the below-threshold route requires an SFC designation and permits a holistic assessment. For example, an in-scope Fund with established aggregate exposure of exactly 50% satisfies the trigger without a separate designation. A Fund at 49% with established absence of an SFC designation does not satisfy this selected trigger merely because its CLO holdings or liquidity profile warrant scrutiny; a Fund at 49% that has actually been designated does satisfy it. An otherwise comparable LAF falls outside this circular's defined Fund scope. A Fund whose exposure or designation history is missing cannot be treated as the established 49%-and-undesignated case. Footnote 7 supports attaching holistic assessment to cases below 50%, rather than making the express 50% threshold discretionary. The strongest uncertainty is how to establish aggregate exposure for layered instruments and the relevant assessment date.","run_id":"run.07ade899f13b40218b344b2eaeb2295c","scheduling_priority":0,"schema_version":"interpretation.v1","score_purpose":"INVESTIGATION_PRIORITY_ONLY","source_packet_hash":"be86c12a28ac1c552b9cc386dfa44174629a63a786068d9bf5d8cdb44cbfa056","source_unit_ids":["d4148dd852cee.u21.3779","d4148dd852cee.u29.4630","d4148dd852cee.u32.4805","d4148dd852cee.u4.564","d4148dd852cee.u49.6955","d4148dd852cee.u63.8691","d4148dd852cee.u64.8910"],"status":"ACTIVE","subject_unit":"Selected control: whether the retained circular triggers complex-product treatment for distribution of a particular Fund"}